SuperMario Odyssey isn't just Mario's  biggest adventure ever or one of the  best titles of 2017 it's also a giant  sprawling love letter to the portly  plumbers video game history Odyssey  might take Mario further than he's ever  been from the Mushroom Kingdom but the  entire journey is absolutely drenched in  callbacks to his long and storied past  just watch out for spoilers this list  goes into just a few of the big  surprises waiting for you a wonderful  wardrobe Super Mario Odyssey lets you  buy a variety of different outfits with  your hard-earned coins that's right if  you've gotten tired of Mario's red and  blue get up or if after 36 years you  figure is simply due for a change of  clothes you can give Mario a makeover  some of the costumes are brand new to  the Mario series but others have pretty  obvious origins the ouija Wario and  Waluigi outfits are all available for  purchase and Mario's classic suit makes  his overalls red and a shirt blue just  like in the very first Super Mario  Brothers you'll also find some fairly  obscure stuff from Super Mario history  the chef's suit recalls Mario's days  baking in Yoshi's cookie the Safari  ready explorer suit is a nod to the Game  Boy puzzler Mario's pick Ross while the  poncho costume resembles Mario's outfit  in the Game Boy edition of quicks as  well as one of his gets ups in his Japan  only anime appearance the painter outfit  references the Super Nintendo tights or  Mario paints the patriotic golf outfit  is from open tournament golf while the  aviator outfit sort of looks like the  clothes Mario wears in his first  portable outing Super Mario Land drawing  that game to shoot him up plane levels  it goes even deeper though and unless  you know Mario's Japanese heritage a few  of these are especially deep cuts  Mario's mechanic outfit is borrowed from  1988's famicom grand prix to 3d hot  rally a japan-only racing game Mario's  fashionable outfit isn't an old  reference but it still weirdly obscure  in 2014 when entender released its new  3ds  it launched a Japanese advertising  campaign starring singer Kyary Pamyu  Pamyu in which Nintendo's classic  characters get brand new clothes  look familiar  celebrating Super Mario maker in 2015  Nintendo rolled out the last 2d Mario  game that anyone would ever need Super  Mario maker the new title flipped the  script and let players officially design  and share their own Mario levels for the  first time and despite appearing on the  underperforming Wii U Super Mario maker  sold over a million copies and boasts  over 7.2 million levels for Mario fans  to enjoy all be impossibly frustrated by  by any measure that's a hit  and one that should keep fans and  amateur game designers busy for years to  come naturally Nintendo put a few  carefully plays to Super Mario maker  Easter eggs and Odyssey like Mario's  yellow and red build a helmet and outfit  which can be purchased a new dong city's  hut shop Super Mario Odysseys other  Mario maker egg is a little more subtle  in some levels you'll run across 8-bit  pictures of Mario and Princess Peach  dressed in cat outfits while the cat  suit first appeared in the Wii U's Super  Mario 3d World the sprites themselves  are from Super Mario maker appearing as  one of the costumes that Mario can wear  in order to unlock the costumes in Super  Mario maker you'll need to clear a  special event in Super Mario wada see  the sprites serve a different purpose  hit them with copy Mario's new hat like  friends and you'll get a small health  boost mario 64 evolved Odyssey owes more  to Super Mario 64 than any other Mario  game since both drop players into wide  open worlds filled with collectibles  platforming is still Mario's bread and  butter but both of those games focus  more on exploration than mechanical  challenges the games are connected by  more than just that though dory the  goggles wearing Loch Ness monster like  creature who floats around the lake  Kingdom made his debut in Super Mario 64  in which players could ride him around  in order to discover new areas in the  wooded Kingdom Mario needs to chase down  some terrified rabbits not unlike a  series of similar rabbit based chases  that take place in Princess Peach's  basement in Super Mario 64 and while  mario stomped his way through various  kingdoms he runs across paintings that  transports him to other worlds which is  a pretty clear reference to Super Mario  64's hanging portraits which serve as  gateways to the games levels and if  there was any doubt Mario's goofy  low-def Mario 64 outfit  here to all Kong all the time most  tomorrow fans know that Nintendo's  mascot first appeared in the company's  1981 hit arcade game Donkey Kong in  which the mustachioed construction  worker had to rescue his girlfriend  Pauline from the big dumb animal the  game's new dong city level is one giant  tribute to that 8-bit ape  Pauline once a damsel in distress is now  nude on city's beloved singing mayor the  city is also full of moving girders and  intrepid explorers will find wooden  barrels just like the kind Donkey Kong  used to throw nude on city streets are  also named after characters from the  Donkey Kong Country series including  relatively obscure ones like Donkey  Kong's animal pals Rambi and rat lay  cranky Kong who is canonically the  original Donkey Kong gets his own Avenue  as well  new dongs City license plates read 1 9 8  1 ND referring to Donkey Kong's release  date and Super Mario odyssey's jazzy  title track a jump up superstar uses the  original Donkey Kong music as a backing  melody and let's not forget about this  when Mario first appeared in Donkey Kong  he was known simply as jump man you  found a power moon every time Mario  finds a power moon  Super Mario odyssey's main collectible  Mario celebrates with a victory pose but  they're not all the same sometimes he  puts up two fingers sometimes he  triumphantly pumps his fist in the air  occasionally he keeps his hand open and  surprisingly there's a little bit of  history behind each one of those poses  the split fingered v sign is what Mario  does after he finds a star in Super  Mario 64 the fist pump hails from the -  Super Mario Galaxy games the open handed  pose comes from Super Mario Sunshine  it's a small touch but it goes a long  way towards honoring Super Mario  odyssey's predecessors after all  Mario wouldn't be where he is without  them toe tapping tunes while Super Mario  Odyssey is full of visual nods to the  series past the game is also full of  auditory callbacks to the past Super  Mario games for example Mario runs  across boom boxes that pump out smooth  jazzy covers of classic Mario tracks if  you use copy to possess the statues in  the sand Kingdom your notice that they  hum little snippets of past Super Mario  soundtracks return to the Mushroom  Kingdom  Odyssey is a big game of lots to do and  of course as with most Mario games  beating Bowser as  the beginning once you defeat King  Cooper and free princess peach the real  challenge begins  not only is every world flooded with a  new set of power moons to hunt down BA  Mario can access a few new kingdoms  including one that looks very very  familiar the Mushroom Kingdom  just like in Mario 64 Mario's home base  has full of things to do with 104 more  power moons to discover which is just  under Mario 64's 120 stars you can  access new challenges through paintings  find a Yoshi hiding on the castle  grounds and even discover a few areas  that look exactly like their 64-bit  counterparts the music is even the same  as he original in addition in a fun  nostalgic throwback the mushroom  kingdoms power moons looked like Mario  64's bright yellow stars  Princess Peach may not be around but it  doesn't really matter after all this  time it's just good to be home  thanks for watching click the loop icon  to subscribe to our youtube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  you're love tea  [Music]
 

